*---------------------------------------------------------------
* byeres.equ -- shared constants between byeres.s (assembled
* STANDALONE at $D100, embedded into procbye.s via putbin --
* the asrom.s/proshimpg.s literal-address idiom) and procbye.s
* (which installs the blob and must reach into it at fixed
* offsets without a shared assembler symbol table -- these are
* two SEPARATE assemblies, so only numeric literals cross).
*
* BYE_ORG and BYE_BLOB_LEN are load-bearing constants, chosen
* up front. The six _A ("address") constants are DERIVED --
* read off byeres.s's own -v1 listing after every edit (docs
* MEMORY note: "Listing addresses are per-build") -- and pinned
* here by hand under names distinct from byeres.s's own labels
* (BYE_LEAVE the equ vs BYE_LEAVE the label would collide in
* ONE assembly). byeres.s carries an `err` tripwire beside each
* labeled cell comparing it against the matching _A constant,
* so a value that drifts out of sync fails THAT assembly loudly
* rather than sending procbye.s to the wrong address silently.
*---------------------------------------------------------------
BYE_ORG      equ   $D100
BYE_BLOB_LEN equ   768        ;exactly what QUIT copies
                              ;($D100-$D3FF)

* -- read off byeres.s's own -v1 listing (2026-09-26 build,
* -- second pass: page-1 save/restore moved to K_BYE_BANK's own
* -- aux $0180-$01FF, and the RESTORE half moved again, into
* -- BYE_START itself (the $1000 trampoline) -- BYE_BACK is LC-
* -- resident and cannot safely flip ALTZP at all, see
* -- docs/BYE-SLICE1.md). BYE_LEAVE_A shifted too this time
* -- (BYE_START grew).
BYE_LEAVE_A   equ  $D138
BYE_BANKNO_A  equ  $D312
BYE_SAVEVLO_A equ  $D313
BYE_SAVEVHI_A equ  $D314
BYE_SAVE80_A  equ  $D315
BB_ARMVEC_A   equ  $D316
BB_RESVEC_A   equ  $D318

* -- 2026-09-26: the second save bank (the annex) and the /RAM
* -- reconnect/redisconnect state -- BYE_BACK's own annex
* -- restore and PRC_RAMREDISC vector. Read off byeres.s's -v1
* -- listing after every edit, same as the six above.
BYE_BANKNO2_A equ  $D31A
BB_HADRAM_A   equ  $D31B
BB_RAMDVEC_A  equ  $D31C

* -- 2026-09-26 slice 2 (docs/BYE.md "Slice 2 launch"): 1 = a
* -- tenant was named on this `bye` -- BYE_LEAVE jumps to
* -- BYE2_ORG (the launch blob, below) instead of the bare-QUIT
* -- trigger. Stamped from PBY_HASTEN, procbye.s. Read off
* -- byeres.s's -v1 listing after every edit, same as the cells
* -- above.
BB_TENANT_A   equ  $D31E

* -- BB_KSGVEC_A: KSEG_RELOAD's real address, stamped by
* -- procbye.s -- appended AFTER every other stamped cell
* -- (byeres.s's own comment at the matching `ds`), so it never
* -- shifts when an earlier cell changes size. Re-derived
* -- 2026-09-27 (docs/KSEG.md round 2): the `jsr BB_KSGCALL` +
* -- `BB_KSGCALL jmp (BB_KSGVEC)` insertion shifted every cell
* -- from BYE_BANKNO_A onward by +6 B -- values above and below
* -- this line are the REAL -v1 listing addresses (`err`
* -- tripwires temporarily disabled to get a clean build, then
* -- restored; every value here checked against that listing,
* -- not hand-derived from the diff).
BB_KSGVEC_A   equ  $D31F

* -- 2026-09-27 (docs/KSEG.md): byelaunch.s moved OUT of this
* -- cross-assembly agreement entirely. It is no longer a
* -- separate `putbin`'d blob at a hand-pinned address -- it is
* -- now a segment MODULE, `put` directly into the same manifest
* -- assembly as procbye.s (playtest.s's `org KSEG_ORG` block),
* -- so procbye.s references its labels (BYE2_START, BL2_PSTG,
* -- ...) as ORDINARY LINKED SYMBOLS. BYE2_ORG, BYE2_BLOB_LEN,
* -- BYE_COMBO_LEN and BL2_PATH_A retire with it -- BYERES is
* -- byeres.bin alone again (768 B, BYE_BLOB_LEN), and the
* -- launch blob is loaded (and RELOADED after every tenant
* -- return) as part of KSEG, not concatenated onto BYERES.
* -- BYE_LEAVE still reaches it with a plain `jmp #KSEG_ORG`
* -- (byeres.s cannot name BYE2_START -- separate assembly --
* -- but KSEG_ORG is a FIXED hardware address, inc/mm.hw.equ,
* -- and the segment's first module always starts there).
